From: Elevator HMI meta-hmi-platform
Subject: [PATCH] drm: panel: jadard -- LMT101 H4a: F0,55/F1,AA/E0,01/E3,01 booster enable

H4a hypothesis test: the FAE BIST sequence writes F0,55/F1,AA/E0,01/E3,01
after DISON; the standard vendor init table (196 cmds) does NOT write E3
on page 1. Page-1 E3 may be the charge pump (JD5001 booster) enable register
that starts AVDD/AVEE/VGH/VGL generation.

Evidence from DIAG15 (patch 0015 result):
  0x0F = 0xC0 -- registers loaded OK, IC logic functional (rules out H4b/H6)
  0x0A = 0x1c -- booster bit 0x80 still OFF (charge pump never started)
  0x45 = 0x00 -- scan not running (consistent with no VGH/VGL)

This patch inserts the 5-command sequence immediately after DISON in the
FAE_CLOCK path, before the existing 50ms settle and 0x0A read. If the booster
starts, dmesg will show GET_POWER_MODE(0x0A) >= 0x9C (bit 7 set) on the next
boot -- confirming H4a and making this sequence the production fix.

F0,55 / F1,AA: Jadard unlock password for protected command registers.
E0,01:         select page 1.
E3,01:         write target register (booster/charge-pump enable candidate).
E0,00:         restore page 0 for TE and normal scanout.

Applies after patches 0001-0015 (requires FAE_CLOCK path from 0011+0013).

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
index b0f77b8228a6..d5d5c4d8ac92 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jadard-jd9365da-h3.c
@@ -177,7 +177,33 @@ static int jadard_enable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 			u8 self_diag;
 			ssize_t rd;
 
-			/* Clean 0x0A read: ~50 ms after DISON, before TE / page churn */
+			/*
+			 * H4a test (PATCH-0016): FAE BIST writes F0,55/F1,AA/E0,01/E3,01
+			 * after DISON; the standard vendor init table does NOT write E3
+			 * on page 1. Page-1 E3 may be the charge pump (booster) enable
+			 * register. F0,55/F1,AA unlock the Jadard protected command set
+			 * before E3 can be written. E0,00 restores page 0 for TE/scanout.
+			 * If 0x0A reads 0x9C after this (booster bit 0x80 set), H4a
+			 * is confirmed and this write sequence is the production fix.
+			 */
+			err = jadard_generic_reg_val(dsi, dev, 0xf0, 0x55);
+			if (err < 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a F0,55 err=%d\n", err);
+			err = jadard_generic_reg_val(dsi, dev, 0xf1, 0xaa);
+			if (err < 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a F1,AA err=%d\n", err);
+			err = jadard_generic_reg_val(dsi, dev, 0xe0, 0x01);
+			if (err < 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a E0,01 err=%d\n", err);
+			err = jadard_generic_reg_val(dsi, dev, 0xe3, 0x01);
+			if (err < 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a E3,01 err=%d\n", err);
+			err = jadard_generic_reg_val(dsi, dev, 0xe0, 0x00);
+			if (err < 0)
+				dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a E0,00 err=%d\n", err);
+			dev_info(dev, "jadard: H4a sent F0,55/F1,AA/E0,01/E3,01/E0,00\n");
+
+			/* Clean 0x0A read: ~50 ms after H4a writes, before TE / page churn */
 			msleep(50);
 			rd = mipi_dsi_dcs_read(dsi, 0x0a, &pwr_mode, 1);
 			if (rd < 0)
